  "last_message": "I implemented `can_cancel`. It returns true only while `now` is at least 2 hours before the pickup slot starts (`larder/cancellation.py:8`). The 2-hour window comes from `docs/features/cancellation.md`, which says volunteers pack the bags in those last 2 hours. I put the number in a named constant, `CUTOFF_HOURS = 2`, the same way `sessions.py` handles its expiry time.\n\n**One choice to check:** the doc says a member can cancel \"until 2 hours before \u2026 and not after\" but doesn't say what happens at exactly 2 hours. I allowed a cancellation at exactly 2 hours. If you want that moment blocked, change `<=` to `<`.\n\nI also added `tests/test_cancellation.py`, which checks a time just before the cutoff, exactly at it, and one second after. All 5 tests pass.",
